  "notes": [
    "descriptor is a concrete declaration-backed JVM descriptor, not a guessed layout. fixedRuntimeDescriptor=null means the exact vendor descriptor has not yet been verified; do not promote it to fixed admission merely from AOSP main.",
    "No new Activity.mToken field is required by the examined source: attachment token is passed as Activity.attach argument 3, while ActivityClientRecord.token is read at launch.",
    "No ActivityClientRecord.activityInfo/packageInfo field is required by the examined launch adapter; do not add unused hidden capabilities.",
    "Physical endpoint must be captured before writing ActivityThread.sPackageManager, ServiceManager.sCache[package], or the existing host ApplicationPackageManager.mPM.",
    "ServiceManager.sCache itself is read as Map; update only the package entry. ContextImpl.mPackageManager is read/replaced per logical Context lookup.",
    "Public compilable methods such as Activity.setIntent(Intent,ComponentCaller), setTheme(int), ContextWrapper.getBaseContext and IInterface.asBinder do not inherently need a new hidden-field registry entry.",
    "Activity/newActivity/performLaunchActivity/attach and ContextImpl.getPackageManager/ServiceManager query methods are interception targets, not call-only entries; their selectors are in /tmp/tripoder-runtime-fixed-targets.json.",
    "The physical IPackageManager list has seven methods. getPackageInfoVersioned is routed by RuntimePackages to its existing logical query and physicalPackageInfo when appropriate; it is not a separate physical bypass in current code."
  ]
